NOTICE for text_detection_en_ppocrv3_2023may.onnx
=================================================

This file is not part of Isocenter's own source code. It is a third-party
model shipped unmodified beside this NOTICE, and it is read by
isocenter/text_detection.py when a configuration says
`burned_in_text: {detector: db}` (#1121).

What it is
----------
PP-OCRv3 English text detection (DB, Differentiable Binarization), fp32,
converted to ONNX by the OpenCV Model Zoo.

  File:    text_detection_en_ppocrv3_2023may.onnx
  Size:    2,423,490 bytes
  sha256:  03f550c6b406fda8bf54bd8327815f6c7e2edd98cea02348c93d879254366587

Isocenter refuses to load any file under this name whose sha256 is not the
one above (isocenter/text_detection.py, MODEL_SHA256), and a test holds the
file, that constant and this NOTICE together.

Where it comes from
-------------------
  Source:   OpenCV Model Zoo, models/text_detection_ppocr
            https://github.com/opencv/opencv_zoo/tree/main/models/text_detection_ppocr
            (the Git LFS object of the file named above)
  Upstream: PaddleOCR, https://github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR
            The zoo's README names the original Paddle model as
            en_PP-OCRv3_det_infer:
            https://paddleocr.bj.bcebos.com/PP-OCRv3/english/en_PP-OCRv3_det_infer.tar

