Training data
-------------
As PaddleOCR documents it for PP-OCRv3 detection, quoted from the paper
(Li et al., "PP-OCRv3: More Attempts for the Improvement of Ultra
Lightweight OCR System", arXiv:2206.03001v2, section "DataSets",
https://arxiv.org/abs/2206.03001):

  "For text detection, there are 127k training images and 200 validation
  images. The training images consist of 68K real scene images and 59K
  synthetic images. The real scene images are collected from Baidu image
  search and public datasets, including LSVT (Sun et al. 2019), RCTW-17
  (Shi et al. 2017), MTWI 2018 (He and Yang 2018), CASIA-10K (He et al.
  2018), SROIE (Huang et al. 2019), MLT 2019 (Nayef et al. 2019), BDI
  (Karatzas et al. 2011), MSRA-TD500 (Yao et al. 2012) and CCPD 2019 (Xu et
  al. 2018). The synthetic images mainly focus on the scenarios for long
  texts, multi-direction texts and texts in table. The validation images
  are all from real scenes."

The paper describes the PP-OCRv3 system as a whole and does not
separate the English detection model's training set from the Chinese one.
The zoo's README also says "`IC15` in the filename means the model is
trained on IC15 dataset" and "`TD500` in the filename means the model is
trained on TD500 dataset"; neither appears in this file's name, so that note
does not describe this file. The datasets carry their own terms; the owner
ruled on shipping this model on 2026-10-15 (Q-C2 of #1121).

How Isocenter runs it
---------------------
Through OpenCV's cv2.dnn.TextDetectionModel_DB (the optional `textdetect`
extra), with binary threshold 0.3, unclip ratio 2.0, input scale 1/255 and
input mean (122.68, 116.67, 104.00), the settings measured on synthetic
MIDI-B data before this file was shipped. Isocenter does not change the
weights.
